lass VR environment, the Physician can trigger SciX queries via voice command (e.g., “SciX: Show similar activation patterns in recent epilepsy studies”), with the results appearing as floating windows next to the live 3D brain model.","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"key":"WYM2YrfCea"}],"key":"Lc0agmB0zq"}],"key":"NL6BknMaqH"}],"key":"nlVSmjA8gY"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“Sensory Re-Calibration”","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"key":"Dzwe2fZFBM"}],"identifier":"sensory-re-calibration","label":"“Sensory Re-Calibration”","html_id":"sensory-re-calibration","implicit":true,"key":"EYZ0wZeQtE"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tactile Mapping: If a user has lost sensation in a limb, the Physician can use syGlass in XR to manually stimulate specific “dead” zones. By “tapping” a virtual neuron in the XR environment, they send a signal to the NESD to trigger a phantom touch for the user.","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"key":"KQ6HHm2H75"}],"key":"GiQ2xZafGj"}],"key":"tuoosc1dBd"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pain Suppression: The Physician can identify “pain circuits” (hyper-active clusters) and use an XR interface to “dim” those regions, sending inhibitory signals to provide immediate relief.","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"KGU2A5YF8E"}],"key":"Kg7lnATIZf"}],"key":"P4IWiYHk80"},{"ty